# Feature 2299, 2026-11-14: a package's module named like a built-in, which is
# why panel 234's R13 names the sorting package `core/slices` and not
# `core/sort`. `use <slices>/sort` binds `sort` as a module of the program's own
# does, and is told the same way; the alias its `guess` writes is built from the
# entry and the path, the angle brackets left out (defect 2368).
use <slices>/sort  #~ builtin_name_taken

function main()
    print(sort.twice(2))
